# severance tools table -- which per-tool config dirs live behind the seal.
#
# THE DEFAULTS severance ships, and the only file severance owns. Additions
# belong in drop-ins (~/.config/severance/tools.d/*), on the /etc/profile and
# /etc/profile.d model: one shipped file for the defaults, one file per
# integrator for its own tools, so ownership is never tangled and an upgrade
# to this file cannot clobber somebody else's row.
#
# Columns, whitespace-separated. Blank lines and full-line # comments ignored.
#
#   tool   the command whose presence gates SEALING the dir (never the export:
#          an env var for an absent tool is harmless, and probing PATH on every
#          `work` invocation is not free)
#   env    the variable pointing the tool at its work dir, or `-` for none.
#          This is a BASE: a launcher that selects per-profile (valet-key
#          does, via its own adapters) overrides it at exec. The base is what
#          a BARE invocation inside a work session gets, so it is the thing
#          that keeps a direct call from falling back to the personal dir.
#   dir    the directory UNDER the enclave config root (work_dir/.config)
#   seal   yes = provision it root:<group> 2770 + default ACL, so the tool's
#          credentials sit behind the SAME kernel wall as the tree; no = the
#          enclave config root's own seal already covers it
#
# A row whose tool is absent is skipped for sealing -- the right thing happens
# if the crumbs are there, and nothing happens if they are not.
#
# tool     env                  dir      seal
claude     CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR    claude   no
gemini     GEMINI_CLI_HOME      gemini   yes
codex      CODEX_HOME           codex    no
gcloud     CLOUDSDK_CONFIG      gcloud   yes
